        "original_id": "1a4974de-bba4-5691-857b-4aa1824b3ce6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Augusta, Georgia; New Orleans\n- Systems: Augusta Canal; New Orleans Outfall Canals; Orleans Canal; 17th Street Canal; London Avenue Canal\n- Structures: Butt Memorial Bridge; levees; floodwalls\n- Water Bodies: Savannah River\n- Roads: 15th Street\n\nFacts:\n- The Augusta Canal is fed by the Savannah River and passes through three levels over approximately 13 miles in suburban and urban Augusta before its water returns to the river at various locations.\n- The Butt Memorial Bridge is a road bridge in Augusta, Georgia, that carries 15th Street over the Augusta Canal.\n- The Orleans Canal, the 17th Street Canal, and the London Avenue Canal together form the New Orleans Outfall Canals.\n- The New Orleans Outfall Canals are lined by 13 miles of levees and floodwalls along the sides of the canals.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
